  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscPat1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'Since your diagnosis, research has become a source of hope for you.
    The more you learn about it, the more surprised you are at how involved patients
    seem to be throughout the research process.


    <b>Patients play an important
    role research, but not until clinical trials begin.</b>


    Is this <b>true</b>
    or <b>false</b>?'
  explanation: Even before clinical trials start, patients play an important role
    in shaping research. While they are not yet participants in this stage, patients
    are informants, contributors, and guides. Their medical data, donated samples,
    advocacy, and lived experiences help researchers choose what to study, explain
    why it matters, and design studies in ways that can truly benefit patients later
    on.
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Patient
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
